diff --git a/Docs/PROTOCOL.md b/Docs/PROTOCOL.md
index a5377fcf7931eba8d0d7323cbd3bfa04951a0919..4c2d83037d4912c6f06a064149f04e6a714797a0
--- a/Docs/PROTOCOL.md
+++ b/Docs/PROTOCOL.md
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 
 ## Transport
 
-- WebSocket, text frames, one JSON object per frame, UTF-8. Path `/ws`. Default port `7331`. The host also serves static pages over HTTP on the same port: `/plan.html`, `/site.html`, `/facilitator.html`.
+- WebSocket, text frames, one JSON object per frame, UTF-8. Path `/ws`. Default port `7331`. The host also serves static pages over HTTP on the same port: `/plan.html`, `/site.html`, `/rules.html`, `/facilitator.html`.
 - Every message has `"t"` (type) and `"v": 1`. Unknown types are ignored and logged; unknown fields are ignored.
 - The host sends `state` to every client at 4 Hz while the clock runs, and at once after any command that changed state. Clients never compute game state; they render.
 - Times: `day` is a float in simulated days from the stage start (`0.0` = the morning of Day 1; the display day is `Math.floor(day) + 1`). `speed` is `"full"` (5 s per day), `"slow"` (20 s per day, during an unresolved event), or `"paused"`.
@@ -13,13 +13,14 @@
 ## Client -> host
 
 ```jsonc
-{"t":"hello","v":1,"seat":"plan"|"site"|"facilitator","client":"web"|"quest","name":"optional"}
+{"t":"hello","v":1,"seat":"plan"|"site"|"rules"|"facilitator","client":"web"|"quest","name":"optional"}
 // reply: {"t":"welcome","v":1,"seat":"...","stage":"stage1_texas","protocol":1,"state":{...}}
 // A second client for a seat that is already taken is accepted as a mirror (read-only) and told so: "mirror": true.
 
 {"t":"cmd","v":1,"id":"c-17","seat":"plan","action":"commit","ops":[ ...PlanOp ]}
 {"t":"cmd","v":1,"id":"c-18","seat":"site","action":"moveTo","stationFt":720}
-{"t":"ctrl","v":1,"id":"c-19","action":"start"|"pause"|"resume"|"reset"|"load","stage":"stage2_texas"}   // facilitator only
+{"t":"cmd","v":1,"id":"c-19","seat":"rules","action":"ready"} // any player seat during a guide beat
+{"t":"ctrl","v":1,"id":"c-20","action":"start"|"pause"|"resume"|"continue"|"reset"|"load","stage":"stage2_texas"}   // facilitator only
 ```
 
 Every `cmd`/`ctrl` gets exactly one `ack` or `nack` with the same `id`.
@@ -77,6 +78,26 @@
 
 **Facilitator** (`seat: "facilitator"`): everything, including hidden variants, pending events and deviations, the two other views side by side. Never shown to players; used by Bryan during table tests and by Playwright during verification.
 
+**Rules** (`seat: "rules"`): exactly `{stage, displayDay, speed}` in `state.view`. No positions, plan, money, daily reports, field events or result overlay. On welcome and reset/load it also receives `kit`: `{t:"kit", v:1, stage, title, job:{sign:{cityCode,pipe,contractDays},lengthFt,zones}, permits:{cards}, inspections:{cards,checklist}, manualPages}`. These are authored job sign, card and ledger facts, not live simulation state. The page loads the filled manual from `manual/<stage>.html`; signatures, checkboxes and ledger notes remain in that page and reset with the run. Rules can send `ready`; simulation commands are unavailable to it.
+
+## Guided playthrough (WO-S7)
+
+The Node host accepts `--guide Data/Guides/slice_guided.json`. The browser host offers Guided and a guide picker. Enabling Guided resets the run and turns Autoplan off; it can be enabled again explicitly. The selected guide must match the selected scenario. Without a guide, the existing clock and commands are unchanged.
+
+On Start, and at each subsequent trigger, the host pauses and sends each player only their own prompt:
+
+```json
+{"t":"guide","v":1,"beat":{"id":"b0_brief","index":0,"count":9,"title":"Morning brief"},"prompt":"Find zone 1's permit card. Check the digits, then read the code to Plan.","rulesSection":"permits_holdpoints","ready":{"site":false,"plan":false,"rules":false}}
+```
+
+`index` is zero-based. Only the facilitator's message adds `narration`, `prompts:{site,plan,rules}`, and `beats:[{id,title,status}]`, where status is `upcoming`, `current`, `done` or `skipped`. No guide source or other seat's prompt is sent to a player. Between beats, `beat` and `rulesSection` are null and `prompt` is empty; player banners hide. The facilitator keeps the beat list. Joining a running guide receives its current message.
+
+Beats trigger in order on start, authored event id, conflict pair (`back-pipe` corresponds to event id `conflict_back_pipe`), simulation time, backfill within 10 ft of a zone end (including idle at the hold point), or result. The host observes the completed simulation tick: conflict events carry the beginning-of-tick time and pause at the end of that 0.01-day tick. If a later trigger fires before an earlier trigger, the earlier beat is skipped. Triggers reached during a paused trip are retained until the current beat ends.
+
+`cmd ready` marks the sending seat ready, broadcasts the updated ready map and acknowledges once. Once every connected primary player seat is ready, the host waits the guide's `resumeDelaySeconds` of real time, then resumes. Read-only mirrors and the facilitator do not count; no connected players means no automatic resume. A newly connected unready seat cancels a pending countdown. Readiness resets for every beat. `ctrl continue` ends the current beat immediately; any already-triggered next beat pauses immediately. Start/Resume cannot bypass a current guide beat. Reset/load cancel pending countdowns. With no active beat, Ready/Continue return `nack: "no guide beat"`.
+
+Commands remain available during guide pauses. A valid Site `moveTo` while paused advances only the simulation travel duration (`|Δft| / 1500 / 24` days), including the fractional final tick, then pauses again. Other commands do not advance the clock. Guided Site receives only `{t:"result",v:1,stage}` at the result; Plan and the facilitator receive the full overlay. Rules receives the result beat, with its own prompt.
+
 ## Daily report timing
 
 At each day boundary the host emits `report` for the day that just ended and advances `reportedLines` for Plan. Site's view is live at all times. This is the one authored asymmetry everything else depends on; do not "fix" it.
diff --git a/Docs/SCENARIO_SCHEMA.md b/Docs/SCENARIO_SCHEMA.md
index 14fd7d4877208d258e1f6134d6eb01a98133d63f..cceda58e1ca4067371e979b8583c55c7b639e747
--- a/Docs/SCENARIO_SCHEMA.md
+++ b/Docs/SCENARIO_SCHEMA.md
@@ -82,3 +82,28 @@
 ## Validation (WO-01)
 
 `node Monitor/src/scenario/validate.js Data/Scenarios/<file>.json` must check: every machine key exists in the catalog; zones tile `[0, lengthFt]` without gaps; `startDay` ≥ 1; permit and inspection cards cover every zone exactly once with distinct codes whose check digits are correct; every `trigger.crew` and `hits` is a crew id; every `options[].check.seat` is `site`, `plan` or `rules`; every `lines[].trigger` is a known trigger; no key anywhere named `whenRight`, `whenWrong`, `correct`, `verdict`; `_validate` keys allowed anywhere and listed in the output so they can be handed to the validators.
+
+## Guide files (WO-S7)
+
+Guides live separately in `Data/Guides/<id>.json`; they control host pauses and prompts, never simulation rules. `slice_guided.json` follows `Docs/PLAYTHROUGH.md`.
+
+| Field | Meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| `schemaVersion` | `1` |
+| `id`, `scenario`, `title`, `source` | guide id, matching scenario id, guide title, source document |
+| `autoResumeWhenAllReady` | boolean; automatically resume after every connected primary player seat sends Ready |
+| `resumeDelaySeconds` | nonnegative real-time seconds between all-ready and resume; Continue bypasses it |
+| `beats[]` | ordered array of the objects below |
+
+Each beat has a unique `id`, `title`, `trigger`, `narration`, `prompts:{site,plan,rules}` and `rulesSection` (an anchor from the stage's `kit.manualPages`). Narration and the combined prompt map are facilitator-only. The host sends each player only that player's prompt.
+
+| Trigger | Fires when |
+| --- | --- |
+| `{"kind":"start"}` | facilitator starts the run |
+| `{"kind":"event","id":"ev_p1"}` | the simulation fires that event |
+| `{"kind":"conflict","pair":"back-pipe"}` | conflict event `conflict_back_pipe` fires; pair is trailing-leader |
+| `{"kind":"t","atLeast":7}` | simulation `t >= atLeast` (t 7 is Day 8) |
+| `{"kind":"holdPoint","zone":1}` | backfill is within 10 ft of that zone's end, or idle at its hold point |
+| `{"kind":"result"}` | the simulation emits its result |
+
+Triggers are latched. Beats remain ordered; an unfired earlier beat is marked skipped when a later beat becomes due. A trigger reached during a paused Site trip waits until the current beat ends. Reset clears readiness, completed/skipped beats and latched triggers. Loading a different scenario disables an incompatible guide. See `PROTOCOL.md` for the message and Ready/Continue behavior.
diff --git a/Monitor/e2e/guided.e2e.js b/Monitor/e2e/guided.e2e.js
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..1306c02b568b159dd5ed09114f591802c4e9ae0c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Monitor/e2e/guided.e2e.js
@@ -0,0 +1,118 @@
+import test from 'node:test';
+import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
+import { mkdir, readFile } from 'node:fs/promises';
+import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';
+import { chromium } from 'playwright';
+import { startHost } from '../src/host/server.js';
+
+const output = fileURLToPath(new URL('../out/guided/', import.meta.url));
+const guidePath = fileURLToPath(new URL('../../Data/Guides/slice_guided.json', import.meta.url));
+const guide = JSON.parse(await readFile(guidePath, 'utf8'));
+const script = JSON.parse(await readFile(new URL('../test/scripts/slice_play.json', import.meta.url), 'utf8'));
+const beatFor = time => time <= 3.8 ? 0 : time <= 4 ? 1 : time < 5 ? 2 : time < 7 ? 3 : time < 8 ? 4 : time < 9 ? 5 : time < 20 ? 6 : 7;
+
+async function clickAck(page, locator) {
+  const reply = page.evaluate(() => new Promise(resolve => {
+    const listener = event => {
+      const message = JSON.parse(event.data);
+      if (['ack', 'nack'].includes(message.t)) { socket.removeEventListener('message', listener); resolve(message); }
+    };
+    socket.addEventListener('message', listener);
+  }));
+  await locator.click(); const message = await reply;
+  assert.equal(message.t, 'ack', message.reason); return message;
+}
+async function perform(pages, { seat, cmd }) {
+  const page = pages[seat];
+  if (seat === 'plan') {
+    for (const op of cmd.ops) {
+      if (op.op === 'enterPermit' || op.op === 'enterInspection') {
+        const permit = op.op === 'enterPermit';
+        await page.locator('#key-zone').selectOption(String(op.zone));
+        await page.locator(permit ? '#permit-code' : '#inspection-number').fill(permit ? op.code : op.number);
+        await clickAck(page, page.locator(permit ? '#enter-permit' : '#enter-inspection')); return;
+      }
+      if (op.op === 'lend') {
+        await page.locator('#lend-machine').selectOption(op.machine);
+        await page.locator('#lend-crew').selectOption(op.toCrew);
+        await page.locator('#lend-days').fill(String(op.days)); await page.locator('#add-lend').click();
+      } else if (op.op === 'hold') {
+        await page.locator('#hold-crew').selectOption(op.crew);
+        await page.locator('#hold-days').fill(String(op.days)); await page.locator('#add-hold').click();
+      } else if (op.op === 'radio') {
+        await clickAck(page, page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Radio again', exact: true })); return;
+      } else throw new Error('Unhandled plan op: ' + op.op);
+    }
+    await clickAck(page, page.locator('#commit')); return;
+  }
+  const controls = { mount: '#mount', dismount: '#mount', listen: '#listen', stopWork: '#stop-work' };
+  if (cmd.action === 'moveTo') {
+    const before = await page.evaluate(() => ({ day: state.day, ft: state.view.truck.stationFt }));
+    await page.locator('#destination').fill(String(cmd.stationFt)); await clickAck(page, page.locator('#move'));
+    await page.waitForFunction(ft => !state.view.truck.moving && state.view.truck.stationFt === ft, cmd.stationFt);
+    const after = await page.evaluate(() => ({ day: state.day, speed: state.speed }));
+    assert.ok(Math.abs(after.day - before.day - Math.abs(cmd.stationFt - before.ft) / 1500 / 24) < 1e-8);
+    assert.equal(after.speed, 'paused');
+  } else if (cmd.action === 'inspect') await clickAck(page, page.locator(`[data-inspect="${cmd.target}"]`));
+  else if (cmd.action === 'confirm') await clickAck(page, page.locator(`button[data-order="${cmd.orderId}"][data-outcome="${cmd.outcome}"]`));
+  else if (controls[cmd.action]) await clickAck(page, page.locator(controls[cmd.action]));
+  else throw new Error('Unhandled site action: ' + cmd.action);
+}
+
+test('Guided slice: three filtered prompts, script actions, Ready, all beat screenshots and result', { timeout: 180_000 }, async t => {
+  await mkdir(output, { recursive: true });
+  const host = await startHost({ scenarioPath: fileURLToPath(new URL('../../Data/Scenarios/slice_texas.json', import.meta.url)),
+    guidePath, port: 0, testMode: true });
+  let browser;
+  try {
+    browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: true });
+    const context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 1400, height: 1000 } });
+    const pages = {}, errors = [];
+    for (const seat of ['plan', 'site', 'rules', 'facilitator']) {
+      const page = pages[seat] = await context.newPage();
+      page.on('pageerror', error => errors.push(seat + ': ' + error.message));
+      await page.goto(`http://127.0.0.1:${host.port}/${seat}.html`);
+      await page.waitForFunction(() => typeof state !== 'undefined' && !!state);
+    }
+    await pages.rules.waitForFunction(() => document.querySelectorAll('#manual-content section').length === 8);
+    assert.equal(await pages.rules.locator('#cards .card').count(), 4);
+    assert.equal(await pages.rules.locator('#day-boxes input').count(), 8);
+    await pages.rules.getByLabel('Permit day zone 1', { exact: true }).fill('1');
+    await clickAck(pages.facilitator, pages.facilitator.locator('#start'));
+    host.core.setFast(true);
+    for (const [index, beat] of guide.beats.entries()) {
+      for (const seat of ['plan', 'site', 'rules']) {
+        const page = pages[seat];
+        await page.waitForFunction(id => LobGuide.current?.beat?.id === id, beat.id, { timeout: 30_000 });
+        assert.equal(await page.locator('#guide-prompt').innerText(), beat.prompts[seat]);
+        const message = await page.evaluate(() => LobGuide.current);
+        assert.equal(message.narration, undefined); assert.equal(message.prompts, undefined);
+        for (const other of ['plan', 'site', 'rules'].filter(other => other !== seat)) assert.equal(await page.getByText(beat.prompts[other], { exact: true }).count(), 0);
+        assert.equal(await page.getByText(beat.narration, { exact: true }).count(), 0);
+        await page.evaluate(() => window.scrollTo(0, 0));
+        await page.screenshot({ path: output + `${index}-${beat.id}-${seat}.png` });
+      }
+      assert.equal(await pages.facilitator.locator('#guide-narration').innerText(), beat.narration);
+      assert.equal(await pages.rules.locator(`#sections [data-section="${beat.rulesSection}"]`).getAttribute('data-highlight'), 'true');
+      assert.equal(await pages.plan.evaluate(() => state.view.trench), undefined);
+      assert.equal(await pages.site.evaluate(() => state.view.budget), undefined);
+      assert.deepEqual(await pages.rules.evaluate(() => Object.keys(state.view).sort()), ['displayDay', 'speed', 'stage']);
+      for (const entry of script.filter(entry => beatFor(entry.t) === index)) await perform(pages, entry);
+      for (const seat of ['plan', 'site', 'rules']) {
+        await clickAck(pages[seat], pages[seat].locator('#guide-ready'));
+        assert.equal(await pages[seat].locator('#guide-ready').innerText(), 'Waiting for the others');
+      }
+      t.diagnostic(`${beat.id}: prompts, actions and Ready checked`);
+    }
+    await pages.facilitator.waitForFunction(() => LobGuide.current.beats.every(beat => beat.status === 'done'));
+    const final = await pages.plan.evaluate(() => result);
+    assert.ok(final.finishDay > 0); assert.equal(final.lost, undefined); assert.equal(final.deviationsCaught, 1);
+    assert.equal(await pages.site.evaluate(() => result.spentUsd), undefined);
+    assert.equal(await pages.plan.locator('#overlay').isVisible(), true);
+    assert.equal(await pages.rules.getByLabel('Permit day zone 1', { exact: true }).inputValue(), '1');
+    await pages.rules.setViewportSize({ width: 390, height: 844 });
+    assert.equal(await pages.rules.evaluate(() => document.documentElement.scrollWidth <= innerWidth), true);
+    assert.deepEqual(errors, []);
+    t.diagnostic(`Guided result t=${final.finishDay}; 27 screenshots in ${output}`);
+  } finally { await browser?.close(); await host.close(); }
+});
